  "title": "Kinderarzt oder Arztkinder?",
  "subtitle": "Compounds: the last word decides the article",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Überblick",
      "title": "Lesson intro",
      "minutes": 40,
      "learn": [
        "A compound is blocks pushed together. The last noun is the base: it gives the article and the plural.",
        "The first block only specifies. Stress sits on the first block: KINDERarzt, not kinderARZT.",
        "Sometimes a linking letter stands between the blocks: Untersuchungsraum (-s-), Patientenakte (-en-).",
        "der Kinderarzt is the doctor. die Arztkinder are the doctor's children. The order changes the meaning."
      ],
